  "experiment": "replication of the skip-per-commit-publication experiment (first run: 2026-10-12_qbhs0-skip-per-commit-publication_ab.json, NOT a win on its error guard)",
  "decision_rule_fixed_before_the_run": "nopub replication (br-qbhs0). Written 2026-10-12 ~18:15Z, after the first nopub A/B (93b86415, NOT a win: its\nerror guard failed 6 vs 1) and before any replication run. This is a new experiment with its own rule. It does not\nre-decide the first one.\n\nSame binaries: base = build19/base3 (main 2dd72851, sha c5c84438); nopub = build25/nopub (2dd72851 +\nnopub_v1.patch, sha 1401e554). paced_swarm.py now records every non-ok call's payload in errors.json.\n\nRuns (60 agents, 300 s, fresh mailbox each, WAL sampled every 5 s):\n  P2 at period 2 s, 5 per arm: base nopub nopub base base nopub nopub base base nopub.\n  P6 at period 6 s, 2 per arm: nopub base base nopub.\n\nDecision:\n  S1. Pooled P2 send p50 and p90 for nopub <= 0.85x base.\n  E1 (error rate). Total P2 client errors for nopub <= base + 5 (over 5 runs per arm). At P6, nopub <= base + 3.\n  E2 (no visibility failures). No nopub error payload mentions a probe miss, a compensating delete, a message\n     that is missing or not visible, or a durability failure. Matched by case-insensitive substrings: \"probe\",\n     \"compensat\", \"not visible\", \"missing\", \"durab\".\n  G1. Pooled P6 send p50 and p90 <= 1.05x base.\n  G2. fetch_inbox pooled p50 <= 1.10x base at both periods.\n  G3. Peak WAL median <= 1.5x base at both periods.\n  C (from the first rule, still required). C1 db lib full with no new failures (the warmup-timing failure is\n     rerun on a normal worker), C2 tools it and conformance pass, C3 visibility test passes.\n\nWIN only if S1, E1, E2, G1-G3 and C all hold. Even then it changes a cross-process publication contract, so it\ngoes to the owner with both A/Bs before landing. Otherwise LOSS / NOT A WIN, reported, not landed.\n",
